(4687143, 672704, 674, '<td valign="top"><u>What I like</u> <br/> <br/>I like the lighting of this image, it gives a good sense of mood and anticipation.<br/>the angle has given the player a larger, meaner appearance ie dont mess with me buddy.<br/> <br/><u>What I dont like </u> <br/>Is that the editing has made the shadows noisy and grimy!<br/>the background is too black I would prefer to see some shadowy figures to give the feeling thiswas a real game and not just a posed shot.<br/>Congratulations on atop 25 finish.<br/>Sulamk</td>', 'What I like  I like the lighting of this image, it gives a good sense of mood and anticipation.the angle has given the player a larger, meaner appearance ie dont mess with me buddy. What I dont like  Is that the editing has made the shadows noisy and grimy!the background is too black I would prefer to see some shadowy figures to give the feeling thiswas a real game and not just a posed shot.Congratulations on atop 25 finish.Sulamk', '2008-05-07 13:31:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4687389, 673524, 61961, '<td valign="top">Sorry I didn''t get a chance to vote in this challenge; surely this would have received a high score from me.  As others have said, great colors and lighting.  Though Colonel Mustard looks a bit oversized...<br/> <br/>In my day, if I remember right, the game pieces were the standard colored tokens.  It was only the murder instruments that were unique (candlestick, rope, etc.).<br/></td>', 'Sorry I didn''t get a chance to vote in this challenge; surely this would have received a high score from me.  As others have said, great colors and lighting.  Though Colonel Mustard looks a bit oversized... In my day, if I remember right, the game pieces were the standard colored tokens.  It was only the murder instruments that were unique (candlestick, rope, etc.).', '2008-05-07 15:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4687394, 673030, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very clever!  And I thought this was an amazing macro shot hehe.  The blur did catch my attention and I liked the brightness and clarity of the pin.</td>', 'Very clever!  And I thought this was an amazing macro shot hehe.  The blur did catch my attention and I liked the brightness and clarity of the pin.', '2008-05-07 15:06:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4687878, 672752, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, you have a very strong image -- it is well balanced and allows the eyes to "go" from the cards to the chips and back.<br/> <br/>Technically, you exhibit great focus and exposure and the shallow dof works very, very well here.  <br/> <br/>Ordinarily, selective desaturation does not "work" for me, but it seems okay here.  It doesn''t jump out at you and scream "selective" but it does seem to make the red parts stand out nicely.  I tried to imagine if it would be better in straight bw or color, but I think this probably works best.<br/> <br/>The only nit I have, and it has nothing to do with the picture is the red border.  Because red is so bold and screams for attention, my eyes are automatically drawn away from the picture to the border.  Not sure if that is the effect you wanted or not.<br/> <br/>Great shot and excellent interpretation of the challenge.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, you have a very strong image -- it is well balanced and allows the eyes to "go" from the cards to the chips and back. Technically, you exhibit great focus and exposure and the shallow dof works very, very well here.   Ordinarily, selective desaturation does not "work" for me, but it seems okay here.  It doesn''t jump out at you and scream "selective" but it does seem to make the red parts stand out nicely.  I tried to imagine if it would be better in straight bw or color, but I think this probably works best. The only nit I have, and it has nothing to do with the picture is the red border.  Because red is so bold and screams for attention, my eyes are automatically drawn away from the picture to the border.  Not sure if that is the effect you wanted or not. Great shot and excellent interpretation of the challenge. Karma', '2008-05-07 17:42:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4687889, 673519, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>ewwww, I HATE, DETEST, LOATHE, DESPISE, FEAR and think snakes are yucky.  But, I''ll look at your shot anyhow.  :)<br/> <br/>compositionally it is strong.  It is well balanced and the blur leads the eyes straight to the snake.  Also, I like the shallow dof, though perhaps if there were just a touch more focus on the snake, it wouldn''t feel quite so out of focus.<br/> <br/>The muted colors give this a sinister, evil feeling.  And the little guy falling off of the ladder (I admit, I almost missed that little touch) is just classic!<br/> <br/>Or maybe it is just because I hate snakes.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat ewwww, I HATE, DETEST, LOATHE, DESPISE, FEAR and think snakes are yucky.  But, I''ll look at your shot anyhow.  :) compositionally it is strong.  It is well balanced and the blur leads the eyes straight to the snake.  Also, I like the shallow dof, though perhaps if there were just a touch more focus on the snake, it wouldn''t feel quite so out of focus. The muted colors give this a sinister, evil feeling.  And the little guy falling off of the ladder (I admit, I almost missed that little touch) is just classic! Or maybe it is just because I hate snakes. Karma', '2008-05-07 17:49:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4687902, 673353, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this shot doesn''t "follow the rules" I don''t think, but that helps add to the chaos of the shot.  Having the balls in the bottom of the shot really give it a nice balance, and the wide angle makes the hand look disporportionatly small -- which is good.  <br/> <br/>Technically, I like the trails that are visible -- it really adds to the feeling of motion in the shot.  Having the table not be green helps the shot too, as I think a green table would really make it to overbearing and bold.  That said, a touch more contrast might really give it a bit more depth and add to the "punch" a bit more.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, this shot doesn''t "follow the rules" I don''t think, but that helps add to the chaos of the shot.  Having the balls in the bottom of the shot really give it a nice balance, and the wide angle makes the hand look disporportionatly small -- which is good.   Technically, I like the trails that are visible -- it really adds to the feeling of motion in the shot.  Having the table not be green helps the shot too, as I think a green table would really make it to overbearing and bold.  That said, a touch more contrast might really give it a bit more depth and add to the "punch" a bit more. Karma', '2008-05-07 17:54:35.000000', NULL, 0),
